# Real gap found and fixed while writing docs/migration.md: this file was
# referenced by README.md's Quick Start ("cp .env.example .env — not
# included yet") but never actually created. Only two env vars are read
# anywhere in src/ (grepped, not guessed) — both optional, since every real
# value can also be passed as a CLI flag to `migrate-company`.

# Target Postgres connection string. Optional — `--database-url` on the CLI
# always wins if passed, and `--dry-run` REQUIRES the explicit CLI flag
# regardless of what's set here (cli.ts refuses to guess for a dry run).
# Only useful as a default for a REAL (non-dry-run) migration command line.
DATABASE_URL=""

# Path to a Google service-account JSON key with read access to the legacy
# spreadsheet being migrated. Optional — `--google-credentials <path>` on
# the CLI always wins if passed.
GOOGLE_APPLICATION_CREDENTIALS=""
